            <ArticleTitle>Denervation of spinal facet joints for treatment of chronic low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>96-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes a neurolytic technique for the denervation of the posterior lumbar spinal facet joints for the treatment of chronic low back pain. Results are reported of a pilot study, using a simple outpatient procedure and achieved relief of pain in 80% of cases. No major complications were encountered.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
